{"name":"Chance of Showers","hex":"#a5bcba","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"chance","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An opportunity or possibility.","Random occurrence; luck."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Happening by chance, casual."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/chance"},{"term":"showers","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["plural of shower"]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["third-person singular simple present indicative of shower"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/showers"}],"entries":[{"title":"Shower","blocks":[{"text":"A shower is a place in which a person bathes under a spray of typically warm or hot water. Indoors, there is a drain in the floor. Most showers are set up to have adjustable temperature, spray pressure, and showerhead nozzle angle. The simplest showers have a swivelling nozzle aimed downward, while more complex showers have a showerhead connected to a hose that has a mounting bracket; this allows the showerer to hold the showerhead by hand to spray the water onto different parts of their body. A showerhead can be installed in a small shower stall or bathtub, with a plastic shower curtain or door."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b7/IMG_Duschender.jpg/330px-IMG_Duschender.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Shower","wikidata":"Q7863"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3e/Dusche-cut-w025-h025.jpg/250px-Dusche-cut-w025-h025.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/3/3e/Dusche-cut-w025-h025.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3e/Dusche-cut-w025-h025.jpg/250px-Dusche-cut-w025-h025.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_camp